      "content": "Okay, I see where you're going with the \"heritage\" and \"traditional\" aspects for Ahmed and Liam. \n\nBut I'm curious about the \"sophistication\" level of the UI. When we look at the design language for someone like Oluwaseun Adeyemi from Nigeria, are we looking at a similar \"traditional/earthy\" approach, or should the design be more \"modern/globalized\" to signal a high-end fintech experience? I want to make sure we aren't inadvertently suggesting that certain cultures prefer \"traditional\" looks while others (like the Western/European ones) are more suited for \"cutting-edge\" or \"premium\" tech interfaces. How do you balance that?",
